hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16529","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Ali ibn Bilal, from people of the Ansar, they said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then we would leave and shoot arrows until we reached our homes, and the landing places of our arrows were not hidden from us."
"16530","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Ali ibn Bilal al-Laythi, he said: I prayed with a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they narrated to me that they used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then they would go out shooting arrows, the landing places of their arrows not hidden from them, until they reached their homes in the farthest part of Madinah."
